# External compass on a GPS mast.
#
# HARDWARE PREREQUISITE: the APM 2.8's onboard magnetometer must be
# disconnected first by cutting the trace on the solder jumper next to the I2C
# port. Setting COMPASS_EXTERNAL alone does not do this -- both magnetometers
# stay on the same I2C bus and the heading is garbage.
#
# COMPASS_ORIENT is deliberately NOT set here. Run ./solve_compass_orient.py
# to measure it; guessing ROTATION_ROLL_180 is how most people get this wrong.
COMPASS_EXTERNAL 1
COMPASS_USE 1
COMPASS_LEARN 0
